## 6. Styling approach

### Methodology

- **Utility-first Tailwind** on elements (project convention: no new CSS modules / styled-components)
- **Global tokens + base** in `src/app/globals.css`
- **Component variants** via CVA + `cn`
- shadcn / Base UI `data-slot` attributes on primitives

### Global styles

`@layer base`: border/outline defaults, `body` background/foreground, `html` `font-sans scroll-smooth`, link `text-inherit`, `img max-w-full`, `:focus-visible` ring using `--ring`.

`@layer utilities`: `.scrollbar-none`, `.heading-page`, `.heading-section`.

Dark variant exists (`@custom-variant dark`) but the storefront ships a **light** paper theme; do not introduce a dark marketing theme unless explicitly requested.

### Responsive design

- Breakpoints: standard Tailwind (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, …)
- Mobile-first class stacks on components (see `HeroSection`, `Container`, headings)
- Touch targets and bag/sheet patterns are mobile-aware; desktop nav is separate from `MobileNavMenu`

### Motion

- `tw-animate-css` imported globally
- Prefer short opacity/transform transitions already used on overlays (`data-starting-style` / `data-ending-style` on Base UI)
- For new motion work, follow the Motion skill / existing overlay patterns — avoid decorative noise

### Code style (UI)

- No semicolons; double quotes; `const` arrows; `handle*` event handlers
- Kebab-case filenames
- Accessibility: labels, `aria-*`, focus rings; E2E prefers roles/accessible names over `data-testid`

